(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the historical development of the C language and its role as the foundation of modern system software.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Historical Evolution and Systems Impact of C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Historical Background:) Tj
T*
(   - Developed between 1969 and 1973 by Dennis Ritchie at Bell Laboratories.) Tj
T*
(   - Evolved directly from Ken Thompson's B language, which was derived from BCPL \(Basic Combined) Tj
T*
(   Programming Language\).) Tj
T*
(   - Designed to provide structured high-level constructs while maintaining low-level memory) Tj
T*
(   access and machine efficiency.) Tj
T*
(   2. The UNIX Operating System Milestone:) Tj
T*
(   - In 1973, Dennis Ritchie and Ken Thompson rewrote the UNIX kernel in C.) Tj
T*
(   - This was revolutionary because operating systems were historically written in assembly) Tj
T*
(   language.) Tj
T*
(   - Rewriting UNIX in C allowed it to be ported across entirely different hardware architectures) Tj
T*
(   by recompiling the C source.) Tj
T*
(   3. Language Standardization Trajectory:) Tj
T*
(   - K&R C \(1978\): Defined by Brian Kernighan and Dennis Ritchie's seminal book 'The C Programming) Tj
T*
(   Language'.) Tj
T*
(   - ANSI C / ISO C90: Standardized in 1989 \(ANSI X3J11\) and 1990 \(ISO/IEC 9899:1990\). Introduced) Tj
T*
(   function prototypes and void pointers.) Tj
T*
(   - C99: Introduced inline functions, variable-length arrays \(VLAs\), stdbool.h, and standard) Tj
T*
(   integer types \(stdint.h\).) Tj
T*
(   - C11/C17: Added multi-threading support, atomic operations, bounds-checking interfaces, and) Tj
T*
(   memory alignment specifications.) Tj
T*
(   4. Role as the Lingua Franca of Systems Programming:) Tj
T*
(   - Forms the core of major operating system kernels: Linux, macOS \(XNU\), Windows NT, Android,) Tj
T*
(   and iOS.) Tj
T*
(   - Powers core runtimes: Python \(CPython\), JVM \(HotSpot\), Node.js \(V8 engine\), and embedded) Tj
T*
(   avionics/biomedical instruments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
