(   Keywords vs User-Defined Identifiers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Contrast:) Tj
T*
(   - Keywords: Fixed vocabulary of the C language grammar \(32 keywords in C89, expanded in) Tj
T*
(   C99/C11\). They are reserved by the language specification and trigger specific compiler) Tj
T*
(   instructions.) Tj
T*
(   - Identifiers: Custom tokens defined by the programmer to identify memory addresses, functions,) Tj
T*
(   types, and labels.) Tj
T*
(   2. Complete List of 32 Standard ANSI C89 Keywords:) Tj
T*
(   auto break case char const continue default do) Tj
T*
(   double else enum extern float for goto if) Tj
T*
(   int long register return short signed sizeof static) Tj
T*
(   struct switch typedef union unsigned void volatile while) Tj
T*
(   3. Strict Identifier Lexical Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - Allowed Characters: Uppercase letters [A-Z], lowercase letters [a-z], digits [0-9], and) Tj
T*
(   underscore [_].) Tj
T*
(   - First Character Rule: MUST begin with an alphabetic letter or an underscore. Numbers as the) Tj
T*
(   first character \(e.g., 2nd_val\) are illegal and cause compiler syntax errors.) Tj
T*
(   - Reserved Keyword Rule: Keywords cannot be used as identifiers \(e.g., int float = 10; is) Tj
T*
(   invalid\).) Tj
T*
(   - Case Sensitivity: C is strictly case-sensitive: Gene, gene, and GENE represent three distinct) Tj
T*
(   identifiers.) Tj
T*
(   - Whitespace and Special Characters: Spaces, punctuation, hyphens \(-\), and symbols \(@, $, %, #\)) Tj
T*
(   are prohibited.) Tj
T*
(   4. Scope and Namespace Isolation:) Tj
T*
(   - Block Scope: Identifiers declared inside { ... } are visible only within that block.) Tj
T*
(   - File Scope \(Global\): Identifiers declared outside functions are accessible throughout the) Tj
T*
(   translation unit.) Tj
T*
(   - Identifier Shadowing: A local identifier masks an identically named global identifier inside) Tj
T*
(   its enclosing block.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
