(   [Problem Statement]: Provide an in-depth breakdown of primitive data types in C, their memory footprints, value ranges, and format specifiers.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Primitive Data Types in C:) Tj
T*
(   C provides fundamental scalar data types mapped directly to underlying microprocessor) Tj
T*
(   architecture registers and memory units.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Character Types:) Tj
T*
(   - char: Represents single ASCII character or small integer. Memory: 1 byte \(8 bits\).) Tj
T*
(   - signed char: Range: -128 to +127. Format specifier: %c \(character\), %d \(integer\).) Tj
T*
(   - unsigned char: Range: 0 to 255. Format specifier: %c, %u.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Integer Types \(Typical 32-bit/64-bit Architecture\):) Tj
T*
(   - short int: Memory: 2 bytes \(16 bits\). Range: -32,768 to +32,767. Specifier: %hd.) Tj
T*
(   - unsigned short: Memory: 2 bytes. Range: 0 to 65,535. Specifier: %hu.) Tj
T*
(   - int: Memory: 4 bytes \(32 bits\). Range: -2,147,483,648 to +2,147,483,647. Specifier: %d or %i.) Tj
T*
(   - unsigned int: Memory: 4 bytes. Range: 0 to 4,294,967,295. Specifier: %u.) Tj
T*
(   - long int: Memory: 4 bytes \(Windows\) or 8 bytes \(Linux/POSIX 64-bit\). Specifier: %ld.) Tj
T*
(   - unsigned long int: Specifier: %lu.) Tj
T*
(   - long long int \(C99\): Memory: 8 bytes \(64 bits\). Range: -9.22e18 to +9.22e18. Specifier: %lld.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Floating-Point Types \(IEEE 754 Representation\):) Tj
T*
