(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the IEEE 754 floating-point standard for single-precision \(float\) and double-precision \(double\) numbers in C.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   IEEE 754 Floating-Point Standard:) Tj
T*
(   Floating-point numbers in C are encoded according to the IEEE 754 international standard,) Tj
T*
(   dividing binary representation into three distinct bitfields:) Tj
T*
(   1. Sign Bit \(S\): 1 bit \(0 = positive, 1 = negative\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Biased Exponent \(E\): Represents scale with an added bias to eliminate explicit negative) Tj
T*
(   exponent signs.) Tj
T*
(   3. Significand / Mantissa \(M\): Represents fractional precision with an implicit leading 1) Tj
T*
(   \(normalized form: 1.M\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Floating-Point Layouts:) Tj
T*
(   1. Single-Precision \(float - 32 bits total\):) Tj
T*
(   - Sign \(S\): 1 bit \(Bit 31\).) Tj
T*
(   - Exponent \(E\): 8 bits \(Bits 30-23\). Exponent Bias: +127.) Tj
T*
(   - Mantissa \(M\): 23 bits \(Bits 22-0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Real Value Formula: \(-1\)^S * 2^\(E - 127\) * \(1 + M / 2^23\)) Tj
T*
(   - Approximate decimal precision: ~6 to 7 significant digits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Double-Precision \(double - 64 bits total\):) Tj
T*
(   - Sign \(S\): 1 bit \(Bit 63\).) Tj
T*
(   - Exponent \(E\): 11 bits \(Bits 62-52\). Exponent Bias: +1023.) Tj
T*
(   - Mantissa \(M\): 52 bits \(Bits 51-0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Real Value Formula: \(-1\)^S * 2^\(E - 1023\) * \(1 + M / 2^52\)) Tj
T*
(   - Approximate decimal precision: ~15 to 17 significant digits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Special Values Defined by IEEE 754:) Tj
T*
(   - Positive / Negative Zero: Exponent = 0, Mantissa = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Subnormal Numbers: Exponent = 0, Mantissa != 0 \(gradual underflow\).) Tj
T*
(   - Positive / Negative Infinity \(+Inf, -Inf\): Exponent = all 1s, Mantissa = 0 \(e.g. 1.0 / 0.0\).) Tj
T*
(   - NaN \(Not a Number\): Exponent = all 1s, Mantissa != 0 \(e.g. 0.0 / 0.0 or sqrt\(-1.0\)\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Precision Pitfalls in C:) Tj
T*
(   Decimals like 0.1 cannot be represented precisely in finite binary fractions) Tj
T*
(   \(0.0001100110011...\).) Tj
T*
(   Comparing floats with == \(e.g. if \(f == 0.1\)\) frequently fails. Must check tolerance: fabs\(a -) Tj
T*
(   b\) < EPSILON.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
