(   [Problem Statement]: Compare #define symbolic constants with const variables and enum types, discussing advantages and limitations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparison: #define vs const vs enum in C:) Tj
T*
(   C provides three mechanisms for establishing immutable constants, each operating at distinct) Tj
T*
(   compilation phases:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. #define Preprocessor Macro:) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanism: Textual find-and-replace performed by preprocessor prior to compilation.) Tj
T*
(   - Syntax: #define BUFFER_SIZE 1024) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages: Zero memory allocation; usable in compile-time static array dimensions in older) Tj
T*
(   C89.) Tj
T*
(   - Limitations: No type safety; invisible to symbolic debuggers \(GDB shows only literal) Tj
T*
(   replacement\); scope cannot be restricted to blocks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. const Variables:) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanism: Statically typed read-only memory locations handled by compiler proper.) Tj
T*
(   - Syntax: const int buffer_size = 1024;) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages: Full type-checking; visible in debuggers with symbol table entries; respects) Tj
T*
(   block scoping rules.) Tj
T*
(   - Limitations: In C89, const variables are not true compile-time constant expressions \(cannot) Tj
T*
(   dimension static arrays: int arr[buffer_size]; was illegal before C99 VLAs\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. enum \(Enumeration Types\):) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanism: Named integral constants defined in symbol table during semantic analysis.) Tj
T*
(   - Syntax: enum { MAX_SIZE = 1024, MIN_SIZE = 16 };) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages: True compile-time integer constant expressions; type-safe; grouped logically;) Tj
T*
(   zero memory overhead unless instantiated.) Tj
T*
(   - Limitations: Strictly restricted to integer constants; cannot define floating-point or string) Tj
T*
(   constants.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Summary Matrix:) Tj
T*
(   Feature #define const variable enum) Tj
T*
(   Compilation Stage Preprocessing Semantic Analysis Semantic Analysis) Tj
T*
(   Memory Storage None \(Literal\) May allocate stack None \(Symbol table\)) Tj
T*
(   Type Safety None Strict Strict \(Integer only\)) Tj
T*
(   Debugger Visibility No Yes Yes) Tj
T*
(   Non-Integer Values Yes \(float/string\) Yes \(float/string\) No \(Integer only\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
