(   [Problem Statement]: Explain logical operators \(&&, ||, !\) and the mechanics of Short-Circuit Evaluation with code demonstrating side-effect traps.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Logical Operators and Short-Circuit Evaluation:) Tj
T*
(   C provides three logical operators operating on boolean truth conditions:) Tj
T*
(   1. Logical AND \(&&\): True if and only if both operands evaluate to non-zero.) Tj
T*
(   2. Logical OR \(||\): True if either or both operands evaluate to non-zero.) Tj
T*
(   3. Logical NOT \(!\): Unary operator that inverts truth value \(0 becomes 1; non-zero becomes 0\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Short-Circuit Evaluation Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   C strictly guarantees left-to-right evaluation of logical expressions and short-circuits as) Tj
T*
(   soon as the final result is determined:) Tj
T*
(   - In expression \(A && B\): If A evaluates to 0 \(false\), the entire expression MUST be false.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, operand B is NEVER evaluated!) Tj
T*
(   - In expression \(A || B\): If A evaluates to non-zero \(true\), the entire expression MUST be) Tj
T*
(   true. Therefore, operand B is NEVER evaluated!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Side-Effect Trap Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int increment_counter\(int *c\) {) Tj
T*
(   \(*c\)++;) Tj
T*
(   return 1;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   int counter = 0;) Tj
T*
(   int a = 0;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Trap 1: Logical AND short-circuit skips function execution */) Tj
T*
(   if \(a && increment_counter\(&counter\)\) {) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Condition Met\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Counter after AND: %d\\n", counter\); /* Outputs 0! Function was skipped! */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
