(   [Problem Statement]: Detail Prefix vs Postfix increment/decrement operators, explaining sequence points and undefined behavior in expressions like i = i++ + ++i.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Prefix vs Postfix Increment/Decrement and Sequence Points:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operational Distinction:) Tj
T*
(   - Prefix \(++x, --x\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Increment/decrement variable x by 1 immediately.) Tj
T*
(   2. Yield the newly updated value as the expression result.) Tj
T*
(   - Postfix \(x++, x--\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Yield the current original value of x as the expression result.) Tj
T*
(   2. Increment/decrement variable x by 1 subsequently.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Code Trace Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   int a = 5, b = 5;) Tj
T*
(   int r1 = ++a; /* a becomes 6; r1 receives 6 */) Tj
T*
(   int r2 = b++; /* r2 receives 5; b becomes 6 */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Sequence Points in C \(C89/C99\) and Sequenced-Before \(C11\):) Tj
T*
(   - A sequence point is a designated point in program execution where all side effects of) Tj
T*
(   previous evaluations are guaranteed to be complete.) Tj
T*
(   - Major Sequence Points:) Tj
T*
(   a. End of a full expression \(at the semicolon ';'\).) Tj
T*
(   b. After evaluating first operand of logical AND \(&&\) or OR \(||\).) Tj
T*
(   c. After evaluating condition in ternary operator \(?:\).) Tj
T*
(   d. Comma operator \(,\).) Tj
T*
(   e. Before a function call executes after arguments are evaluated.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Undefined Behavior in: i = i++ + ++i:) Tj
T*
(   - ISO C Standard Rule: Between consecutive sequence points, an object shall have its stored) Tj
T*
(   value modified at most once by expression evaluation. Furthermore, the prior value shall be) Tj
T*
(   accessed only to determine the value to be stored.) Tj
T*
(   - Analysis of i = i++ + ++i:) Tj
T*
(   Here, variable 'i' is modified multiple times \(by i++, by ++i, and by assignment =\) without an) Tj
T*
(   intervening sequence point!) Tj
T*
(   Different compilers \(GCC, Clang, MSVC\) produce wildly conflicting outputs \(e.g., 7, 8, 9\).) Tj
T*
(   The C standard classifies this strictly as UNDEFINED BEHAVIOR. Compilers are permitted to) Tj
T*
(   generate any machine code or crash.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
