(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the mechanics of printf\(\), explaining conversion specifiers, minimum field width, precision, and alignment flags.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mechanics and Formatting Options of printf\(\):) Tj
T*
(   The standard library function printf\(\) outputs formatted text to stdout according to format) Tj
T*
(   specifications:) Tj
T*
(   Syntax: int printf\(const char *format, ...\);) Tj
T*
(   Return Value: Returns total number of characters successfully printed, or negative value on) Tj
T*
(   error.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Structure of Format Specifier:) Tj
T*
(   %[flags][width][.precision][length]specifier) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Core Conversion Specifiers:) Tj
T*
(   - %d / %i: Signed decimal integer.) Tj
T*
(   - %u: Unsigned decimal integer.) Tj
T*
(   - %f: Decimal floating-point \(default 6 decimal digits\).) Tj
T*
(   - %e / %E: Scientific exponential notation \(e.g. 1.23e+04\).) Tj
T*
(   - %c: Single character.) Tj
T*
(   - %s: Null-terminated character string.) Tj
T*
(   - %x / %X: Hexadecimal representation \(lowercase/uppercase\).) Tj
T*
(   - %p: Pointer address in hexadecimal.) Tj
T*
(   - %%: Literal percent sign.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Flags:) Tj
T*
(   - '-' \(Minus\): Left-align output within given field width \(default is right-align\).) Tj
T*
(   - '+' \(Plus\): Force sign display \(+ or -\) for signed numbers.) Tj
T*
(   - '0' \(Zero\): Pad with leading zeros instead of spaces.) Tj
T*
(   - ' ' \(Space\): Insert space before positive values to align with negative values.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Minimum Field Width and Precision:) Tj
T*
(   - Width: Specifies minimum number of character columns reserved.) Tj
T*
(   printf\("%8d", 42\); /* Outputs: ' 42' */) Tj
T*
(   printf\("%-8d", 42\); /* Outputs: '42 ' */) Tj
T*
(   printf\("%08d", 42\); /* Outputs: '00000042' */) Tj
T*
(   - Precision \(.N\):) Tj
T*
(   - For floats: Number of decimal places: printf\("%.2f", 3.14159\) -> '3.14') Tj
T*
(   - For integers: Minimum number of digits to print \(leading zeros added\).) Tj
T*
(   - For strings: Maximum number of characters to output: printf\("%.4s", "Biotechnology"\) -> 'Bio') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
