(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the mechanics of scanf\(\), explaining the address-of operator &, return values, and buffer clearing for character inputs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mechanics, Pitfalls, and Buffer Handling in scanf\(\):) Tj
T*
(   The scanf\(\) function reads formatted input from standard input \(stdin\):) Tj
T*
(   Syntax: int scanf\(const char *format, ...\);) Tj
T*
(   Return Value: Returns number of input items successfully matched and assigned; returns EOF on) Tj
T*
(   end-of-file or early read failure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Role of the Address-Of Operator \(&\):) Tj
T*
(   In C, parameters are passed by value. To allow scanf\(\) to store converted inputs directly into) Tj
T*
(   caller variables, memory addresses must be provided:) Tj
T*
(   int age;) Tj
T*
(   scanf\("%d", &age\); /* Passes memory location of age */) Tj
T*
(   Exception: Strings/arrays decay to pointers automatically \(e.g., char str[50]; scanf\("%s",) Tj
T*
(   str\); does not require &\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Trailing Newline \('\\n'\) Buffer Bug:) Tj
T*
(   When reading numbers, scanf leaves the trailing Enter key \('\\n'\) in the stdin input buffer.) Tj
T*
(   If a subsequent scanf\("%c", &ch\) is executed, it immediately consumes the leftover '\\n' without) Tj
T*
(   waiting for user input!) Tj
T*
(   Code Demonstration of the Bug:) Tj
T*
(   int id; char grade;) Tj
T*
(   scanf\("%d", &id\); /* User types '101' and presses Enter */) Tj
T*
(   scanf\("%c", &grade\); /* Immediately reads '\\n', failing to read user's grade! */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Robust Solutions to the Input Buffer Problem:) Tj
T*
(   - Solution 1: Leading space in format string:) Tj
T*
(   scanf\(" %c", &grade\); /* Leading space skips all whitespace including '\\n' */) Tj
T*
(   - Solution 2: Flushing the buffer with getchar\(\):) Tj
T*
(   int c; while \(\(c = getchar\(\)\) != '\\n' && c != EOF\); /* Clears leftover line */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Validating scanf\(\) Return Value:) Tj
T*
(   Always check return value to prevent undefined behavior from uninitialized variables:) Tj
T*
(   if \(scanf\("%d", &val\) != 1\) {) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Error: Non-numeric input encountered.\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(   return 1;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
