T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Comma Operator: Operator vs Separator:) Tj
T*
(   In C, the comma character performs two entirely distinct grammatical functions:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. The Comma as a Syntactical Separator:) Tj
T*
(   Used to separate items in lists without creating sequence points or operator semantics:) Tj
T*
(   - Variable declarations: int a = 1, b = 2, c = 3;) Tj
T*
(   - Function parameter lists: void compute\(int x, double y, char z\);) Tj
T*
(   - Function argument calls: printf\("%d %d\\n", a, b\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
