(   2. The Comma as an Operator:) Tj
T*
(   - Characteristics: Binary operator possessing the LOWEST precedence \(Level 15\) in the entire C) Tj
T*
(   language.) Tj
T*
(   - Associativity: Strictly Left-to-Right.) Tj
T*
(   - Sequence Point: A guaranteed sequence point exists between the evaluation of the left and) Tj
T*
(   right operands.) Tj
T*
(   - Behavior: Evaluates left expression, discards its result, then evaluates right expression and) Tj
T*
(   returns its value and type.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Code Demonstrations:) Tj
T*
(   - Example 1: Basic evaluation) Tj
T*
(   int x = \(5, 10, 15\); /* Evaluates 5, then 10, then 15. x is assigned 15 */) Tj
T*
(   - Example 2: In loop control statements \(most common valid use-case\)) Tj
T*
(   for \(i = 0, j = 10; i < j; i++, j--\) {) Tj
T*
(   /* Executes multi-variable increments within a single for-loop header */) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Parentheses Importance:) Tj
T*
(   Because the comma operator has lower precedence than assignment \(=\):) Tj
T*
(   int a;) Tj
T*
(   a = 1, 2, 3; /* Grouped as \(a = 1\), 2, 3. Variable a receives 1! */) Tj
T*
(   int b = \(1, 2, 3\); /* Grouped as b = \(1, 2, 3\). Variable b receives 3! */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
