/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the Ternary Conditional Operator \(?:\), comparing its syntax and performance with if-else branching.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Ternary Conditional Operator \(?:\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Syntax and Operation:) Tj
T*
(   The ternary operator is C's sole three-operand operator, offering an inline conditional) Tj
T*
(   expression:) Tj
T*
(   Syntax: condition ? expression_if_true : expression_if_false) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Key Distinction from if-else:) Tj
T*
(   - if-else is a control-flow STATEMENT: it executes code blocks but does not yield a value.) Tj
T*
(   - \(?:\) is an EXPRESSION: it evaluates and returns a computed value, allowing direct assignment) Tj
T*
(   or embedding inside expressions and macro definitions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Code Example:) Tj
T*
(   /* if-else statement approach */) Tj
T*
(   int max_val;) Tj
T*
(   if \(a > b\) max_val = a;) Tj
T*
(   else max_val = b;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Ternary expression equivalent */) Tj
T*
(   int max_val = \(a > b\) ? a : b;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Nesting and Associativity:) Tj
T*
(   Associativity: Right-to-Left \(Level 13\).) Tj
T*
(   Can be chained to emulate else-if ladders:) Tj
T*
(   char grade = \(score >= 90\) ? 'A' :) Tj
T*
(   \(score >= 80\) ? 'B' :) Tj
T*
(   \(score >= 70\) ? 'C' : 'F';) Tj
T*
ET

