(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to compute the molecular weight of a single-stranded DNA oligonucleotide given nucleotide base counts.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Oligonucleotide Molecular Weight Computation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Biological and Physical Background:) Tj
T*
(   Average molecular weights of deoxyribonucleotide monophosphates \(dNMPs\) in ssDNA:) Tj
T*
(   - dAMP \(Adenine\): 313.21 g/mol) Tj
T*
(   - dCMP \(Cytosine\): 289.18 g/mol) Tj
T*
(   - dGMP \(Guanine\): 329.21 g/mol) Tj
T*
(   - dTMP \(Thymine\): 304.20 g/mol) Tj
T*
(   - Net water removal for phosphodiester bonds: Subtract \(N - 1\) * 18.015 g/mol, plus 17.01 g/mol) Tj
T*
(   for 5' monophosphate/terminal groups.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   #define MW_A 313.21) Tj
T*
(   #define MW_C 289.18) Tj
T*
(   #define MW_G 329.21) Tj
T*
(   #define MW_T 304.20) Tj
T*
(   #define MW_WATER 18.015) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   double compute_oligo_mw\(int a, int c, int g, int t\) {) Tj
T*
(   int total_bases = a + c + g + t;) Tj
T*
(   if \(total_bases == 0\) return 0.0;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   double raw_sum = \(a * MW_A\) + \(c * MW_C\) + \(g * MW_G\) + \(t * MW_T\);) Tj
T*
(   /* Correct for water loss during condensation polymerization */) Tj
T*
(   double adjusted_mw = raw_sum - \(\(total_bases - 1\) * MW_WATER\);) Tj
T*
(   return adjusted_mw;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   int count_A = 6, count_C = 4, count_G = 8, count_T = 6;) Tj
T*
ET

