BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the layout of standard C header files, explaining include guards \(#ifndef, #define, #endif\) and library linking.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Header Files, Include Guards, and Multi-File Compilation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose of Header Files \(.h\):) Tj
T*
(   Header files establish interface contracts between program components by declaring:) Tj
T*
(   - Function prototypes \(signatures and parameter types\).) Tj
T*
(   - Global macro definitions \(#define\) and enumerations \(enum\).) Tj
T*
(   - User-defined composite structures \(struct, union, typedef\).) Tj
T*
(   - Extern variable declarations.) Tj
T*
(   They contain no executable function definitions \(to avoid duplicate symbol linker errors\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Multiple Inclusion Problem:) Tj
T*
(   If header file A.h includes Common.h, and B.h also includes Common.h, then a source file main.c) Tj
T*
(   including both A.h and B.h will receive duplicate struct declarations, resulting in fatal) Tj
T*
(   compilation errors: 'redefinition of struct'.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Include Guard Solution \(#ifndef / #define / #endif\):) Tj
T*
(   Wrap every header file with preprocessor conditional guards:) Tj
T*
(   /* Begin Header File: bioseq.h */) Tj
T*
(   #ifndef BIOSEQ_H_INCLUDED) Tj
T*
(   #define BIOSEQ_H_INCLUDED) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Function prototypes and data types */) Tj
T*
(   typedef struct {) Tj
T*
(   char id[32];) Tj
T*
(   int length;) Tj
T*
(   } SequenceMetadata;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   double compute_mw\(const char *seq\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   #endif /* BIOSEQ_H_INCLUDED */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Modern Alternative \(#pragma once\):) Tj
T*
(   Supported by almost all modern compilers \(GCC, Clang, MSVC\). Non-standard but widely used) Tj
T*
(   directive placed at the top of headers to instruct preprocessor to open the file only once.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Linking Header Declarations with Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   Including a header \(#include <math.h>\) only supplies function prototypes to the compiler. The) Tj
T*
(   actual binary machine code implementation must be linked during the linking stage \(e.g. gcc) Tj
T*
(   main.c -lm\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
